{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EDCoherentLocality","lean:module:QOU.Optimization.LagrangianCollisionFlow","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.peak_dual_antitoneOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.peak_dual_antitoneOn","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L315-L322","doc":"Along the peak-normalised approach the dual value is a monotone function of\nthe angle: it decreases as `γ` grows on `[0, π]`, and equals `g(μ★)` at `γ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.dual_monotoneOn_ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.dual_monotoneOn_ray","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L288-L313","doc":"**The dual value increases along the segment to a maximiser.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.peakMultiplier_selects_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.peakMultiplier_selects_free","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L278-L286","doc":"**Negative result for the peak normalisation**: if the free word `a` is\nactive at `μ★` (as it is when `μ★` sits on the wall between `a` and the ILP\nword), then for every `0 < γ ≤ π` and `n ≥ 1` the selected word at\n`peakMultiplier μ★ n γ` is `a`, never the ILP word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier_selects_free_of_kernel_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier_selects_free_of_kernel_lt","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L272-L276","doc":"The same, for any `γ` with `K_n(γ) < 1` (the exact switch condition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier_selects_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier_selects_free","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L265-L270","doc":"**Far from coincidence the free word is selected** (kernel normalisation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier_selects_ilp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier_selects_ilp","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L252-L263","doc":"**Near coincidence the ILP word is selected** (kernel normalisation):\nif `i` is active at `μ★` with dominant reading, `1 ≤ n` and `(n+1) γ² < 4`,\nthen `i` is the unique active word at `edMultiplier μ★ n γ`, and stays active\non a neighbourhood of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.active_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.active_le","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L247-L250","doc":"`i` active at `μ★`, in the `∀ j` form used above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.ray_mem_cell_above","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.ray_mem_cell_above","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L232-L245","doc":"Beyond `μ★`: a word `i` active at `μ★` whose reading `μ★ ⬝ x i` strictly\ndominates every other word's is the unique active word for every `t > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.ray_mem_cell_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.ray_mem_cell_below","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L215-L229","doc":"Below `μ★`: the strictly cheapest word `a`, if still active at `μ★`, is\nthe unique active word on the whole segment `[0, μ★)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.peakMultiplier_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.peakMultiplier_zero","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L211-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier_zero","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L207-L209","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.edMultiplier","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L203-L205","doc":"Kernel-normalised multiplier: `μ(γ) = K_n(γ) • μ★`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.peakMultiplier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.peakMultiplier","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L199-L201","doc":"Peak-normalised multiplier: `μ(γ) = p_n(γ) • μ★`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_gt_one_of_near","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_gt_one_of_near","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L169-L193","doc":"**Explicit inner radius**: `K_n(γ) > 1` once `1 ≤ n` and `(n+1) γ² < 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_lt_one_of_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_lt_one_of_far","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L147-L167","doc":"**Explicit outer radius**: `K_n(γ) < 1` once `32 < (n − 1) γ⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.quad_le_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.quad_le_pow","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L126-L145","doc":"`(1+s)^n ≥ 1 + n s + n(n−1)/2 s²` for `s ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_tendsto_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_tendsto_zero","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L108-L124","doc":"**Locality**: for a fixed angle `0 < |γ| ≤ π`, `K_n(γ) → 0` as `n → ∞`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_le","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L104-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_antitoneOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_antitoneOn","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L100-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_zero","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L97-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L94-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.kernel","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L90-L92","doc":"Reproducing kernel of the spin-`n/2` coherent states for the normalised\nround measure: `K_n(γ) = (n+1) cos^{2n}(γ/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.overlap_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.overlap_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L80-L88","doc":"Strictly below `1` away from coincidence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.overlap_antitoneOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.overlap_antitoneOn","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L68-L78","doc":"**Monotone in the angle**: `p_n` decreases on `[0, π]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.overlap_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.overlap_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L64-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.overlap_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Optimization.EDMultiplier.overlap_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Optimization/EDMultiplier.lean#L61-L62","signatureChunk":0}]}